{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dtdh59wtAPGEoVbj7NVoti","type":"tool_result","content":"a searcher and remove it again before clearing anything, which recontaminates\nnothing. On $K_{1,3}$, placing and removing a searcher on each leaf before\nguarding the centre is an optimal recontamination-free strategy for which the\nclaim fails.\\lean{kirousisPapadimitriou_claim2_false} The theorem is true. The\nrepair orders the vertices by clearing time, as our Lean proof does, or uses the\npaper's own normal form, its Corollary~2.4.\n\n\\subsection{A thirteenth member}\n\nProgressive black-white pebbling, which is not in Table~1, belongs to the exact\ncore. \\citet[Thm~3]{LY2002ref14} gives\n$\\vs(G)\\le K\\iff\\mathrm{pbw}(G_d)\\le K+2$ on the dag $G_d$ built from $G$; his\nTheorem~2 gives $\\mathrm{pbw}(D)=\\vs(D_u)+1$ on a dag $D$, where $D_u$ is the\nMOSP graph of the matrix whose column $v$ is $v$ with its predecessors; and the\nminimum progressive pebbling number of \\citet[Thm~3.1]{LY2002ref10} equals\n$\\pw+1$. All three are proved in Lean, each with its hypothesis: Lengauer's\nTheorem~2 in its instance form fails at $K=1$ on a dag with no arcs, and\n$\\mathrm{mpb}=\\ns$ fails on edgeless graphs.\\lean{pbw_lengauerD_eq_pathwidth, pbw_eq_mospValue_pebbleMatrix, mpb_eq_pathwidth_add_one}\n\n\\paragraph{Summary.} Seven of Table~1's twelve problems are pathwidth, or\npathwidth plus one, exactly: MOSP, gate matrix layout, one-dimensional logic,\ninterval thickness, node search, narrowness and vertex separation, with pathwidth\nitself as the reference. So are two variants, multiple folding and Lengauer's\nvertex separator game. Split bandwidth and edge search are bands of width one\nand two, which meet the literal reading of Table~1 and not the fixed offset.\nSimple PLA folding and edge separation are false as stated. One theorem is\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/Pebbling.lean:920:theorem pbw_lengauerD_eq_pathwidth {a b : V} (hab : G.Adj a b) :\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/Pebbling.lean-921-    pbw (lengauerD G) = pathwidth G + 2 := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/Pebbling.lean-922-  rw [pbw_lengauerD G hab, vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/Pebbling.lean-923-\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/Pebbling.lean-924-/-- `pbw(G_d) = VSG(G) + 2` for every graph with an edge: Theorem 3 as a number. -/\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean:709:theorem pbw_eq_pathwidth_lengauerU_add_one [Nonempty α] :\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean-710-    pbw D = pathwidth (lengauerU D) + 1 := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean-711-  rw [pbw_eq_vertexSeparation_lengauerU_add_one, vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean-712-\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean-713-/-- `pbw(D) = VSG(G_u) + 1` when `D` has an arc between two distinct vertices: Theorem 2 as a\n--\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean:1116:theorem mpb_eq_pathwidth_add_one [Nonempty V] : mpb G = pathwidth G + 1 := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean-1117-  rw [mpb_eq_vertexSeparation_add_one, vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth]\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean-1118-\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean-1119-theorem mpbw_eq_pathwidth_add_one [Nonempty V] : mpbw G = pathwidth G + 1 := by\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean-1120-  rw [mpbw_eq_vertexSeparation_add_one, vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ca66775-dfcf-48ff-8c1d-165e759ce432","uuid":"5966db84-79f4-4df0-a4e2-e3c601a622a9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T08:05:02.840Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"a searcher and remove it again before clearing anything, which recontaminates\nnothing. On $K_{1,3}$, placing and removing a searcher on each leaf before\nguarding the centre is an optimal recontamination-free strategy for which the\nclaim fails.\\lean{kirousisPapadimitriou_