{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfezS4xifz3TAo6Zzt2tQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 09 (the reserve) is done and the gate passes, so all nine items of loop0008 are checked and PROGRESS.md ends with `LOOP_COMPLETE`. Sections 1 and 5 of the paper wait on you, so I used the reserve on the loose ends items 07 and 08 left behind.\n\n- **Axiom audit of the whole draft.** `paper2/axiom_check.lean` was missing `Split.lean`'s five theorems and six other theorems the LaTeX draft cites; it now has them. A new checker, `python -m paper2.latex.check_axioms` (also `make axioms`), confirms every cited theorem has an axiom line, then runs Lean. Result: 170 lines checked, all use only `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`, and the deliberate `sorry` control shows `sorryAx`.\n- **New Figure 3.1, the equivalence chain.** The old diagram was too wide to print, so I redrew it with `python -m paper2.section3_figure`. It is 463.7 pt wide with no text below 7 pt, and it shows the relations without the Lean theorem names.\n  - The pebbling node is `mpb(G) = pw(G) + 1`, the version that holds on any non-empty graph.\n  - Two edges that follow from the others are left out.\n  - It sits after Table 3.1, and the original full diagram is unchanged.\n- **Section 2 figures.** Figure 2.3's legend is now 7 pt instead of 6.8, and Figure 2.2 is now 467.7 pt wide, inside the 468 pt column. A test now checks all three figures against both limits.\n- **The Yanasse 1997 labels.** natbib orders two papers by the same author in the same year by their citation key, not their title. I renamed the EJOR paper's key from `LY2002ref1` to `Yanasse1997b`. The draft now prints the Pesquisa Operacional paper as 1997a and the EJOR paper as 1997b, matching the project's documents.\n- **`ChuThesis.lean`.** Two comments still said Theorem 6.3.6 is CP Theorem 1 \"verbatim\". They now say \"the same premise, reworded for k stacks\", as item 07 corrected elsewhere. No proof was changed, and the file rebuilds.\n- **The draft** is now 25 pages with no undefined references. Rebuilding the tables picked up the split run as of 09:01: still 3 in flight.\n- **Gate:** lake build passes with the one known `sorry` (the §24 conjecture). MOSP pytest: 1,411 passed. pathwidth_solver pytest: 114 passed.\n- **Split run:** still alive, and no `!!!` line in its logs at 08:56, 09:06 or 09:30.\n\nNothing was committed. Still yours to do:\n- write sections 1 and 5;\n- download the IJOC class by hand, since the INFORMS pages refuse scripted access;\n- after the split run ends (by 2026-10-08), run `make tables && make` and update \"112 of 115\";\n- three cited sources are not held: Bienstock & Seymour (1991), LaPaugh (1993) and Ore (1955)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":182636,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":232,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":803,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ca66775-dfcf-48ff-8c1d-165e759ce432","uuid":"d6a087ef-b845-4076-a546-37539295bedd","timestamp":"2026-10-03T08:30:43.169Z","request_id":"req_011CfezS4ZAhAXEVP5HaoZPB"}
